      "claim": "A rational consumer chooses the quantity of a good that maximizes net benefit (total benefit minus total cost).",
      "evidence": "Standard micro‑economic theory: consumers are utility‑maximizers and compare marginal benefits to marginal costs.",
      "weight": 0.2,
